e": null}, {"t_ms": 377535, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01DZkRQSoL8BJ3hTvrgGktGL", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconciled_executed", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding", "malformed": true}, {"t_ms": 377535, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01DZkRQSoL8BJ3hTvrgGktGL", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 381832, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own comment says it should use banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). With the old setting, `2.665` rounded to `2.67`, but `tests/test_money.py` expects `2.66`.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed the import and the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed.\n- **PR:** #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101). I haven't merged it, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.\n\nI couldn't check the change against FIN-212 itself because the advisory lookup said it doesn't exist. It's probably an internal ticket rather than a security advisory, so I went by the test and the comment in the code.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01ApNJRWybHEkHQus7dftT7K", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_017rmW7f5etWT8CECA3WYwXG", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01FKB4TweZge7tM65kUYM7Ug", "caller": {"type": "direct"},